{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>For I am HaShem your Elohim.</b> That is, the Israelite nation is singled out for holiness and purity, for HaShem did not choose to be called Elohim except for Israel; therefore one must distance oneself from impurity." "<b>And you shall sanctify yourselves, etc.</b> That is, if you sanctify yourselves, I will sanctify you so that no abominable thing shall enter your bodies — along the lines of what they said (Ḥullin 5a) that the Holy One, blessed be He, does not bring, etc., and all the more so the righteous themselves. And the Tosafot established this statement with regard to a forbidden substance entering a person's body, for the Holy One, blessed be He, will guard him in this." "<b>Further,</b> it intends: <b>And you shall sanctify yourselves</b> — make fences and barriers lest you become impure, and through this I assure you that you will be holy. And He returned to explain in what matter they will be holy, and said <b>for I am holy</b> — behold, that which makes the reason for their being called holy dependent on Himself, this teaches that His Shekhinah rests upon those who separate themselves, and therefore they are called by His name. And His saying <b>and you shall not defile yourselves</b>, etc. — meaning, besides the things you take upon your mind to guard yourself from, I further assure you that no kind of evil shall befall you, which is His saying ״בְּכָל הַשֶּׁרֶץ הָרוֹמֵשׂ״, etc. It further alludes that through the observance of this commandment, the עַכּוּ״ם will not have dominion over the people of Israel; the עַכּוּ״ם are called שְׁרָצִים וּשְׁקָצִים הָרוֹמְשִׂים עַל הָאָרֶץ."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {2 "עַכּוּ״ם is the standard abbreviation for עוֹבְדֵי כּוֹכָבִים וּמַזָּלוֹת (idolaters); kept the abbreviated form as written by Or HaChaim."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:55:34.310119406Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}